  "question": {
    "text": "A Carnot engine with efficiency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math> takes heat from a source at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. In order to increase the efficiency to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, keeping the temperature of sink same, the new temperature of the source will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>360</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>900</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Efficiency of Carnot engine is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>sink</mi></msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>source</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></math></p><p>Given: Initial efficiency&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>600</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mn>600</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p>When efficiency is increased to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>,</p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;new temperature of source&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>300</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>300</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>.</p>"
  }
}